{
  "id": "COMPOUND:11153 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Propamidine is implicated in the interaction with NH-6 through multiple pathways, all of which converge on the enzyme 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This enzyme is a target of both Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which are both targeted by Propamidine. The shared target of these enzymes with NH-6 suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of a key metabolic or regulatory pathway. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Propamidine exerts its effects through a common intermediate, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which in turn interacts with NH-6. The consistent scores across the paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Propamidine influences the activity of the SDR family or the demethylase is not fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets pointing to the same end point supports the hypothesis that Propamidine may act through a shared pathway to modulate NH-6, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise molecular interactions.",
